    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1570">

                <pb facs="1264" n="1148" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1148"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 819.00/410.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-06-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 19, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Authorization is requested by the supervisory committee to call upon Tenth
                    Infantry Regiment and Marines Battalion in case, contrary to expectations, their
                    assistance should become necessary to preserve order in Panama City and Colon on
                    election days, June 30 and July 14. Committee recommends withdrawal of marines
                    from the Isthmus should not take place before July 14.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dodge.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
